SWEET CHG MON (patch 0298, resident iOS session, user 2026-11-11): after the 10 phase-3 samples the 30 s CNFG_09 watcher (patch 0287, stage 3) also logs one battery row per tick for the rest of the boot, `SWEET CHG MON: t=..s current=.. uA vcell=.. mV`, so tools/resident can apply its battery floor and "falling" rule while the phone stays in iOS. READS ONLY: the same two MAX77759 fuel-gauge registers (0x36: 0x0a Current, 0x09 VCell) and conversions as p3_sample, after the watcher checked the phase-1 gate; no new chip or controller register (the transfer path is chg_i2c_read, as in 0284/0287). A failed read logs `SWEET CHG GAP: MON fuel-gauge read failed`; like every failed read since 0284 it stops the bus, so the next watcher tick ends phase 3 with its own GAP (the host sees no more rows = no battery data). Active only where 0287 stage 3 runs (sweetchgi2c=1 sweetchgicl=900, the xrun default). Applies after 0287. Host test: tools/test_chg_mon.py.

diff --git a/bsd/dev/sweet_chg_i2c.c b/bsd/dev/sweet_chg_i2c.c
index c4bd4c2..94e5c0a 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_chg_i2c.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_chg_i2c.c
@@ -841,6 +841,30 @@ p3_sample(uint32_t t_s)
 	}
 }
 
+/*
+ * Patch 0298 (resident iOS session, user 2026-11-11): one battery row per watcher tick (30 s) for the whole boot, so the host can apply the
+ * battery floor and the "falling" rule (tools/resident). Reads only, the same two fuel-gauge registers and conversions as p3_sample
+ * (0x36: 0x0a Current, 0x09 VCell); the phase-1 gate was checked by the caller. A failed read stops the bus (chg_i2c_read sets i2c_dead), so
+ * the next watcher tick ends phase 3 with its own GAP; this row logs the GAP that names the fuel gauge.
+ */
+static void
+mon_row(uint32_t t_s)
+{
+	uint8_t cu[2], vc[2];
+	int32_t cs;
+	uint32_t v;
+
+	if (chg_i2c_read(0x36, 0x0a, 2, cu) != 0 || chg_i2c_read(0x36, 0x09, 2, vc) != 0) {
+		(void)i2c_wr(I_INTEN, 0);
+		i2c_log("SWEET CHG GAP: MON fuel-gauge read failed at t=%us: bus stopped, no more battery rows this boot\n", t_s);
+		return;
+	}
+	(void)i2c_wr(I_INTEN, 0);
+	cs = (int16_t)(cu[0] | ((uint32_t)cu[1] << 8));
+	v = vc[0] | ((uint32_t)vc[1] << 8);
+	i2c_log("SWEET CHG MON: t=%us current=%d uA vcell=%u mV\n", t_s, (int)((cs * 3125) / 10), (uint32_t)(((uint64_t)v * 78125u) / 1000000u));
+}
+
 static void
 i2c_p3_tick(int log_pending)
 {
@@ -927,6 +951,7 @@ i2c_p3_tick(int log_pending)
 				p3_done("watcher stopped");
 				return;
 			}
+			mon_row((uint32_t)((p3_next_ms - p3_t0_ms) / 1000u));
 		}
 		p3_next_ms += P3_SAMPLE_MS;
 	}
